# T44298 (264) Management_NTP - IPv6 NTP Server -- working log, run 1

Run label: **clean**.

## Session facts

As T33399 and T33400 (same group, same dispatch): testbox **tb277**, console **u2 ONLY**, PDU
10.36.230.212 outlet u2=1, u2 = **swi_d** (DUT). Sentinel: the parent `/test-mode` session.
Window partly attended. 🔴 swi_a must not be rebooted (and cannot be reached).

🔴 **Both partner consoles (u3 swi_b, u5 swi_a) have a locked `manager` account** and were never
opened by this run -- not even a bare CR. **There is no `swi_b.cfg` and no `swi_a.cfg`**: a
console-lockout limitation, not a bench gap. The NTP client that measures this server is the
**testbox itself**, over IPv6 from `eth3`, which is a better instrument than a partner switch
because it reads every field of every reply.

