VERDICT: PASS -- the x960-56YSQ serves IPv6 NTP exactly as TPS row 262 claims, proven on the wire: three IPv6 requests unanswered with no configuration, then mode-4 replies at the configured stratum 7 with the origin timestamp echoed and a 122 microsecond offset, one capture showing a single `ntp master` serving IPv4 and IPv6 at once with 5 of 5 requests paired, `ntp restrict default-v6 serve deny` silencing every IPv6 client while IPv4 kept being served, silence again after `no ntp master`, and the saved configuration -- both the global IPv6 address and the server itself -- back on the wire 11 s after a cold boot with nothing typed into the device.
